From: podothecat
Subject: [PATCH] egismoc: don't leave task_ssm parked when waiting for a finger fails

An aborted or timed-out verify kills fprintd outright:

    libfprint-egismoc:ERROR:../libfprint/drivers/egismoc/egismoc.c:1908:egismoc_open:
    assertion failed: (self->task_ssm == NULL)
    fprintd.service: Main process exited, code=dumped, status=6/ABRT

In the *_WAIT_FINGER state the parent task_ssm is parked, waiting for the wait-finger
SSM to call fpi_ssm_next_state() on it once a finger arrives. If that SSM instead fails
-- a cancelled verify, or its own "Timed out trying to detect finger on sensor" --
egismoc_wait_finger_ssm_done() reports the action error directly and never touches the
parent. The action ends, the device may then be closed, but self->task_ssm is still
set, so the next egismoc_open() trips the assertion and takes the whole daemon down.

Observed on 1c7a:0588 (ROG Xbox Ally X), reproducible every time: abort a verify, then
claim the device again from the same fprintd process. Clients see the daemon vanish as
"failed to claim device: GDBus.Error:org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.NoReply: Remote peer
disconnected". The attempt after that succeeds, because D-Bus activates a fresh
fprintd -- so the failure alternates and reads as flaky hardware rather than a crash.

Fail the parent SSM instead, and let egismoc_task_ssm_done() clear the pointer and
report the error exactly once. Both functions take ownership of the GError, so it is
handed to exactly one of them.

egismoc_open(), egismoc_cancel() and egismoc_close() are byte-identical between
libfprint 1.94.10 and the egismoc-sdcp fork, so this is not fork-specific.
---
 libfprint/drivers/egismoc/egismoc.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/egismoc/egismoc.c b/libfprint/drivers/egismoc/egismoc.c
--- a/libfprint/drivers/egismoc/egismoc.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/egismoc/egismoc.c
@@ -360,7 +361,23 @@ egismoc_wait_finger_ssm_done (FpiSsm   *ssm,
   self->wait_finger_start = 0;
 
   if (error)
-    fpi_device_action_error (device, error);
+    {
+      /*
+       * The parent task_ssm is parked in *_WAIT_FINGER waiting for this SSM to call
+       * fpi_ssm_next_state() on it. Reporting the action error directly leaves it
+       * parked forever: the action ends, the device can then be closed, but
+       * self->task_ssm is still set, so the next egismoc_open() aborts the whole
+       * process on g_assert (self->task_ssm == NULL).
+       *
+       * Fail the parent instead and let egismoc_task_ssm_done() clear the pointer and
+       * report the error exactly once. Both take ownership of the GError, so it must
+       * be handed to exactly one of them.
+       */
+      if (self->task_ssm)
+        fpi_ssm_mark_failed (self->task_ssm, error);
+      else
+        fpi_device_action_error (device, error);
+    }
 }
 
 static void
